Z||000000||JohnnyK||07-07-2001||04:08 PM||||Anyone in the Toronto area have paintball guns or accessories they want to sell? me and my buddies are thinking of playing (not in an actual place, just with us in a forest or something).. How much could I get a cheap, used gun for?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||07-07-2001||04:35 PM||||Paintball rules. I'll ask my friends if they have any half-decent equipment for sale...<BR>Shipping should be too bad from Winnipeg.<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-07-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||maryjane||07-07-2001||05:23 PM||||I've never been too interested in pointing a gun of any kind at anyone, Vietnam kinda changed the way I looked at things, but my better half has been wanting to give it a try.(anything to keep her happy). Is there any danger of serious injury? Does it hurt much to get shot? Excuse my ignorance, never been out to the painball course to se em play.<BR>don<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Paintball rules. I'll ask my friends if they have any half-decent equipment for sale...<BR>Shipping should be too bad from Winnipeg.<P>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-07-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||07-07-2001||05:42 PM||||With no eye-protection, you can lose an eye to it. I've been many times, and the worst injuries I've had are as follows:<BR>-small, nickel-sized bruises from paintballs<BR>-cut up lip from when one hit the "breather" on my face mask. Very minor, but the paint balls taste like what I'd imagine ****  to taste like  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>-sprained ankle. DAMN GOPHERS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>-Badly injured pride.<P>They don't hurt much, kind of like having a small pebble tossed at you, but not hard. Hard enough to make the spot a little numb, and possibly bruise, but not seriously. <BR>Best approximation I can give is a "lazy fingers" slap, only smaller.<BR>Just make sure you use face/eye protection, and the worst injury you'll get is from running into a tree *NO COMMENT*||||reg||6
Z||000004||Jake_Dragon||07-07-2001||09:09 PM||||When I was in the Navy we used them for training, nothing hurts as much as being an E-3 in 30 degree weather.<BR>Guess who gets to go in first.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||07-07-2001||09:31 PM||||Idon't know, that"RUNNING INTO A TREE(NO COMMENT)"sounds pretty painful! Guess we're gonna try it anyway. Someday that girl's gonna get me crippled!<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 2.5<BR>not slow not fast-just halfast||||reg||12
Z||000006||Mach10||07-08-2001||12:30 PM||||It's a fun <I>game</I>. Nothing to it. As far as my own meandering experience is concerned, it's not really a paintball <I>gun</I>. More of a garden hose. Takes 3 shots to hit someone: <BR>1st to determine range<BR>2nd to determine angle/inclination<BR>3rd to actually try and hit the guy/gal||||reg||7
Z||000007||FieroSTETZ||07-08-2001||01:37 PM||||a bunch of friends and i went out, and we organized into classes, i had a gilly suit on and was a sniper, was doing really well, and decided it would be a good idea to stand up in yonder tree... well, someone from our opposite team goes wandering under and i see him, and wait until hes farther away so i can shoot him.. he walks for a sec, then whirls and "pop" i am pelted in the nuts (had a foot on each of 2 branches) i fell out of the tree - paintballz can hurt!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mach10||07-08-2001||02:40 PM||||Oh yes, I'd forgotten about that.<BR>GUYS: You'd do well to wear a cup. Seriously. ||||reg||7
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||07-08-2001||03:04 PM||||in early June, a guy at my old high school (my sister's a senior there) allegedly made a "hit list", and was planning to bring some guns to school to kill a few people that had been mistreating him. it all turned out ok I guess, the police were warned and the kid was arrested.. but also, the kids who had been bullying him for years were also arrested! (woohoo.. they're a**holes.)<P>anyway, my irrelevant point was, the cops interviewed this guys friends, and when they asked what the kids liked to do, one of them responded that they like to go out in the woods with their guns and play wargames.. that raised a few eyebrows.. LOL.. they didn't mention that they were PAINTguns.. idiots... (see? told ya it was irrelevant.. hehe)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
